ASSET INTEGRATION RULES

Do not use every generated asset.

Use imagery sparingly.

The generated material is a visual vocabulary, not a sticker pack.

Paper tearing must communicate surface vs engine.

Red marker elements should highlight conceptual moments, not decorate empty space.

Architectural photography should support the philosophy/reinvention sections.

Chaos collage should appear only where operational fragmentation is being discussed.

Technical diagrams must be recreated as HTML/SVG rather than baked into images.

All important typography must remain real HTML.

All project metrics and labels must remain editable HTML.

If an image contains imperfect generated typography, crop, obscure, or overlay it with real DOM typography.

Optimize raster assets:
- WebP/AVIF for photography
- PNG only when transparency is required
- responsive image sizing